// The accepted differences between the migrations of the providers that share an id (ADR-0001 W2).
// MigrationContentsTests compares the Up and Down operations of every such migration by kind, table and column, with the
// nullability of columns, the uniqueness of indexes, the on-delete action of foreign keys and the text of SQL (see
// MigrationContents for what is not compared). Every difference needs exactly one entry here. An entry that matches no
// difference fails the check as well.
//
// - "provider" is the provider that has the operation, or the providers separated by ", ".
// - "operation" is exactly as the check prints it. SQL is named by a hash of its text, with white space runs made one space,
//   followed by the start of that text.
// - "category": EquivalentSql (SQL that does what the other providers' operations do), EngineSpecific (a step that only one
//   engine needs) or LegacySqliteData (a fix for data that only old SQLite databases can hold, on SQLite only).
//   A fix for a bug in current code is not a category: it has to reach every provider's migration.
